is exists, then becomes version 3).\n./README.md:28:The folder/mirror are therefore idempotent and original tracks remain untouched. REAPER-native click-source items have no file to clone, so choosing a click track mirrors nothing. `vgt apply` validates the project path and directs you to this action rather than silently falling back to unsafe RPP editing.\n./README.md:32:Use a copy of any project when experimenting; the included `test/Reaper Project` fixture is read-mostly.\n./README.md:34:For a repeatable live-REAPER run against a disposable copy of that fixture, see\n./README.md:36:checks the saved RPP and sidecar after both the first apply and re-apply.\n./README.md:40:`vgt analyze [project.rpp]` requires a `.vgt` sidecar already written by the\n./README.md:42:runs the tempo/key/sections/chords detectors, and writes the results back\n./README.md:43:into the sidecar as schema version 3 — never inside REAPER itself.\n./README.md:49:be corrected by hand-editing its `value` in the sidecar and setting\n./README.md:53:`verified_at`, so the sidecar retains when vgt learned or a human confirmed it.\n./README.md:75:next to the sidecar — a bare click on the detected beat grid (the reference\n./README.md:77:the reference in REAPER; it is vgt-owned and regenerated each run, not\n./README.md:112:`<project>.vgt-chords.txt`, next to the sidecar — a plain-text timestamp +\n./README.md:127:### Sections\n./README.md:129:The `sections` stage detects song-structure boundaries + generic labels\n./README.md:130:(\"A\", \"B\", …) from the reference track's full mix, stored in the sidecar as\n./README.md:144:  recurring section (e.g. a chorus) gets the same label each time.\n./README.md:148:`human_verified: true` is set. Every run also renders a **section-timeline\n./README.md:149:artifact** — `<project>.vgt-sections.txt`, next to the sidecar — so the\n./README.md:155:Run the same ReaScript again after `vgt analyze`. It reads the sidecar and adds\n./README.md:156:`[vgt]` section regions plus a muted `[vgt] Chords` track whose text items\n./README.md:162:When REAPER still has exactly its single default 120 BPM / 4/4 tempo marker,\n./README.md:165:`[vgt] Beats` item track. Both the regions and vgt tracks are reconciled on\n./README.md:166:re-apply; no non-`[vgt]` track, region, or item is changed.\n./README.md:172:  --baseline \"test/Reaper Project/Reaper Project.RPP\"\n./README.md:175:To run the full disposable REAPER proof (including both the default-map and\n./README.md:179:## Correcting chords in REAPER\n./README.md:182:by hand in the sidecar is awkward. Instead, edit the chords directly on the\n./README.md:188:- **split** an item (REAPER's native split action) to break one chord into two;\n./README.md:193:in REAPER's Action List and run it (or run `vgt read-chords [project.rpp]`\n./README.md:195:— position, length, take name — by GUID against the sidecar's\n./README.md:197:writes them back into the sidecar as `analysis.chords.value.segments` with\n./README.md:200:analysis stage (tempo, key, sections) or the rest of the sidecar.\n./README.md:204:identically from the corrected sidecar — the round trip is idempotent.\n./README.md:208:`vgt status [project.rpp]` is read-only: it prints the project and sidecar,\n./README.md:210:timestamps, and the click/chord-sheet/section-timeline artifacts. In\n./README.md:212:human-corrected. Old sidecars that predate timestamps show `unknown` rather\n./pyproject.toml:4:description = \"Non-destructive REAPER project plumbing for virtual guitar teacher\"\n./pyproject.toml:29:# MSAF is the primary section-segmentation backend (docs/GOAL.md), but its\n./pyproject.toml:32:# it. When unavailable (or it fails to import/process), the sections stage\n./tests/test_sections.py:6:from vgt.sections import (\n./tests/test_sections.py:7:    SectionDetectionError,\n./tests/test_sections.py:10:    detect_sections,\n./tests/test_sections.py:53:def test_detect_sections_requires_an_existing_source_file(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n./t